  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With the advent of the Steam Input 2.0 update, there are even more ways that people can move their fingers around. It would be very useful if there were 8 individual float parameters provided by the client that would report an overall curl of each finger. 1: fully curled, 0: neutral, -1: curled backwards (in that slight way that fingers do).\n\nThis would make it easier to make systems that work well across disparate control methods, as well as allow for completely custom hand animations for perhaps not-quite-humanoid avatars. It would also make interactions like pulling a trigger on a gun more easily implemented for different controller types.",
